{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And Moses stretched out his hand, etc.</b> Even though the verse says ״וַיּוֹלֶךְ ה׳ etc. וַיָּשֶׂם אֶת הַיָּם לֶחָרָבָה,״ He did not make [all of] it dry land but only the deep waters — so that not all the waters of the sea would split and Israel would need to descend into the depths and prolong their walking and exertion. Therefore He first sent the east wind to congeal the depths of the water, and this is what it says (Exodus 15:8): ״קָפְאוּ תְהוֹמוֹת בְּלֶב יָם״; and the part that did not congeal was split, and if not for this reasoning there would have been no need for the east wind." "Now one must know when the stretching out of Moses' hand was — whether at the beginning of the night or at its end. From the plain sense of the verse it is evident that it was before morning, and it is difficult, for if so there is no acknowledgment that the splitting of the Sea of Reeds was through Moses. Therefore one is compelled to say that the meaning of the verse is: ״וַיֵּט מֹשֶׁה״ etc. — and HaShem had already led etc. and made the sea dry land; and therefore when he stretched out his hand the waters split, and accordingly, immediately upon his stretching out his hand the sea split. This aligns with what I explained in the verse (Exodus 14:15): ״מַה תִּצְעַק אֵלָי״ — that he did not stretch out his hand except after Israel's journeying, and immediately upon Israel's entry into the sea he stretched out his hand and they split. And so it is in the Midrash Rabbah (Exodus Rabbah 21), and this is its language: ״Immediately, when Moses lifted his hand over the sea, it split,״ end quote. Or it may mean by saying <b>וַיָּשֶׂם אֶת הַיָּם לֶחָרָבָה</b>, that all the waters of the sea congealed, and with the stretching out of Moses' hand the congealed waters split by a measure such that they would not need to descend into the depths of the sea; and in any case the east wind made all the waters of the sea into dry land. And the first interpretation is primary." "<b>All the night.</b> Meaning, until the end of the night, and then the sea split and Israel descended at the morning watch."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "This is a second comment block at index 1 in the source, appearing to continue from comment 0. It contains multiple stacked interpretations with Or it may mean."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:04.646127107Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}